course: dictionary
lesson: 13265
title: Goalmouth: where the action is
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A goalmouth is the area right in front of the goal, between the goalposts. You can work out its meaning from the words around it: «The ball bounced around in the goalmouth.» Ball, goal and bounced all point to a place near the goal.
explain: «The keeper dived to save the shot in the goalmouth.» What word would fit in place of goalmouth? The area in front of the goal. That makes sense, so you have worked it out.
explain: Match reports use goalmouth for a messy fight close to goal. «There was a goalmouth scramble after the corner.» A scramble is a rushed, messy struggle, so the words tell you the players were crowded together and fighting for the ball.
fact: A goalmouth is the area right in front of the goal, between the goalposts.
fact: «Goalmouth» is a noun: one goalmouth, two goalmouths.
fact: You will find goalmouths in football (soccer), hockey and similar games.
fact: A goalmouth scramble is a messy fight for the ball in front of the goal.
fact: Useful phrases are goalmouth action and in the goalmouth.
exercise: «The striker fired the ball into the goalmouth.» Where did the ball go? | Out for a throw-in | *The area right in front of the goal | Into the changing room | The middle of the centre circle
exercise: «The defenders cleared the ball out of the goalmouth.» What does goalmouth mean? | The bench where the substitutes sit | The corner flag | The side line of the pitch | *The area between the goalposts, in front of the goal
exercise: Ella says, «A goalmouth scramble sounds like a cooking game.» What is a goalmouth scramble? | A calm walk to the corner flag | A long pass to the far end of the pitch | *A messy fight for the ball in front of the goal | A game of hide and seek
test: «There was a goalmouth scramble, and nobody could get the ball clear.» What is a goalmouth scramble? | *A messy fight for the ball in front of the goal | A free kick from the halfway line | A slow stroll around the pitch | A quiet rest during half time
test: Which word means the area between the goalposts, in front of the goal? | Penalty spot | *Goalmouth | Halfway line | Touchline
exam: Which sentence uses goalmouth correctly? | *«The keeper caught the ball in the goalmouth.» | «She read the goalmouth before bedtime.» | «The goalmouth was a cold drink on a hot day.» | «The goalmouth sang a song in assembly.»
